    "lawCode": "Amd §§2, 3 & 7, Chap 493 of 1987",
    "lawSection": "Volunteer and Exempt Firefighters' Benevolent Assoc., Inc.",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6262\n\nSPONSOR: WEIK\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 493 of the laws of 1987 creating the Ocean Beach\nVolunteer and Exempt Firefighters' Benevolent Association, Incorporated\nand providing for its powers and duties, in relation to its purpose and\nthe use of foreign fire insurance premium taxes\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 493 of the laws of 1987 creating the Ocean Beach\nVolunteer and Exempt Firefighters' Benevolent Association, Incorporated\nand providing for its powers and duties, in relation to its purpose and\nthe use of foreign fire insurance premium taxes.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends sections 2, 3 and 7 of chapter 493 of the laws of 1987,\nwhich created the Ocean Beach Volunteer and Exempt Firefighters' Benevo-\nlent Association, Incorporated, to update the definition of membership\nin the corporation, as well as expanding the purposes of the corporation\nto include the health and safety of members, enhance moral, and promote\nrecruitment and retention of members.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill has been introduced at the request of the Ocean Beach Volun-\nteer and Exempt Firefighter's Benevolent Association (OBVEFBA).\n\nInsurance Law Sections 9104 and 9105 impose a two-percent tax on premi-\nums paid to foreign fire insurance corporations. These funds are then\ndistributed to the benevolent who serves the properties within the\nservice area. Chapter 493 of 1987, which created the OBVEFBA, severely\nlimits the use of these funds. This bill would expand the use of these\nfunds for more current purposes and uses. This would increase both the\nhealth, recruitment, and retention of members in this fire department\nbenevolent association.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately; provided, however, that the\namendments to section 7 of chapter 493 of the laws of 1987 creating the\nOcean Beach Volunteer and Exempt Firefighters' Benevolent Association,\nIncorporated and providing for its powers and duties made by section one\nof this act shall apply to taxes due on premiums received on and after\nJanuary 1, 2024.\n",
